[212] indent=0 block=-
[213] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "I can go, I guess. Yeah. I think I'm pretty much done with the "
[214] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "initial opic setup. I got a couple of PRs still out, but I think "
[215] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "I've taken care of everything we need to do in the first Kind of "
[216] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "like the first wave. Um The hallucination race... He's like... It "
[217] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "claims to be like 45%, which is... Probably completely wrong, but "
[218] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "this is also symmetrical to the-so the brain trust evaluator was "
[219] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "the faithfulness score. That was coming from around 60%. So it's "
[220] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "like, oh, there's our opposite metrics, and they are also the "
[221] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "inverse measurements."
[222] indent=0 block=-
[223] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "So they could be right, I guess. Um... Yeah. So I think what's "
[224] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "next on the OPEC front would be to I start getting these running "
[225] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "regularly. So I'm thinking about setting up a-I don't know, I "
[226] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "could do-Twice a week. or something measurements against dev or "
[227] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "whatever's in main, I guess. Yeah, so I guess I'm thinking about "
[228] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "like dev and main as the same thing, right? That'll get all "
[229] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "deployed from... main hint to dev."
[230] indent=0 block=-
[231] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "So do that and then probably start working on I guess trying to "
[232] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "measure Like... The quality of the hallucination score, like I "
[233] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "think maybe like an F1 score or something for hallucination "
[234] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "metric. I suspect what we're going to end up with is every time we"
[235] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "laid up one of these metrics that we're going to have to go and "
[236] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "implement it. we'll have to like validate the score that's "
[237] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "producing. Then we get the real score for our system and then we "
[238] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "can start improving the score for our system."
[239] indent=0 block=-
[240] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "So that's kind of what's in my head at the moment for evals. All "
[241] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "this stuff that was going on on the... DataFrame snapshots and the"
[242] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "analytical agents front. Joel has an RFC. for handling snapshots "
[243] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "within EQ Warehouse. It looks good. So now we just have to get "
[244] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "them to actually go build it. But that's kind of like paused all "
[245] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "the rest of the work on that front. Um, And then the other thing "
[246] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "I've been kind of working on is starting to think about expanding "
[247] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "the the kind of chat protocol, like the connection between front "
[248] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "and back end to be able to support, you know, asking for "
[249] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "clarification or asking user approval."
[250] indent=0 block=-
[251] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "So. So yeah, I started working on that. Thank you. You know, I had"
[252] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "a question about the snapshot store thing. So, um, I haven't been "
[253] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "following it closely, but... Each snapshot creates a Databricks "
[254] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "table. That is what Joel is proposing."
[255] indent=0 block=-
[256] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "So what's the user experience like when user asks like a question "
[257] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "that like ends of what agent showing like a data frame user gets "
[258] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "like a link to go to a Databricks table and like gets to yeah like"
[259] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "what's the umLike,..."
[260] indent=0 block=-
[261] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "The idea is that we'll be able, like not every EQ Warehouse call "
[262] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "is going to get saved. You have to actually ask her to like, you "
[263] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "know, Run this query and save it as a table. And then you get back"
[264] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "the identifier of the table. And then you can go and you can use "
[265] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "that in a new query and you can iterate and iterate and each one "
[266] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "can be saved as a separate table. We have these identifiers and we"
[267] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "can returnThat's like tool details, like that kind of citation "
[268] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "back to the client. We're not going to show that table name to the"
[269] indent=6 block=34cdbe27
      "user. We're not going to show them a link."
